{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "6c7e14dd-d79e-5655-b36a-79947562024e",
  "Description": "A chassis on four motorised wheels drives into a stack of boxes.\n\nThe four wheels are one [RigidBody] with a point per wheel. One [RigidJoint] of type Hinge with AutoAnchor puts a hinge at every wheel, and MotorSpeed turns it. [RigidBodyPoints] splits the world's poses up again, so the chassis, the wheels and the boxes are each drawn with their own mesh.\n\nAKA: vehicle, wheels, motor, hinge, drive\n\nTips\n- MotorSpeed is in radians per second; its sign sets the direction.\n- The chassis and wheels share CollisionGroup 1 so the wheels can sit inside the wheel arches.\n- Friction on the wheels is what turns their spin into motion.",
  "InputUis": [],
